    "created_at": "2019-09-08T15:29:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-08T15:29:16Z",
    "body": "Thank you for your feedback @chipbuster \r\n\r\nBefore I open a PR, I would like to describe my train of thoughts just in case I oversaw something.\r\n\r\nI have the feeling that the `integration_test` might be an unnecessary abstraction.\r\nIt contains only two relevant instructions and only the second one has to be executed on a regular basis. \r\n\r\nI would propose to get rid of `integration_test `and instead provide instruction in the CONTRIBUTING.md:\r\n\r\n1. [Link](https://docs.docker.com/install/) to docker installation instructions\r\n2. Instruction to build image\r\n3. Instruction to run test suite\r\n\r\n+ Notes regarding SELinux\r\n\r\nThere should be no loss of convenience as you still only have to execute one command on a regular basis. ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
